  "note": "Urban district election, 18 September 1946; two wards, 15 seats (5 East, 10 West). Labour's three nominees (F. Lyttle, D. Lyttle and W. J. G. Baines) were all returned; H. Anderson and W. J. Dobson stood as individual aspirants."
